# Look before asking David to look

The file browser is an IIFE. The CSS that runs is the `FILE_BROWSER_CSS` string in `file-browser.plugin.ts`. `file-browser.css` is not loaded.

`just remarkable` rebuilds plugins, then the app may copy them on launch. A source edit stays invisible until `~/Library/Application Support/com.markable.app/plugins/core/file-browser.js` contains it.

Before telling him to restart:

- Render the row with that CSS and read the picture.
- Confirm the built file has the new rule and has dropped the old one. The stray dot beside V was `.vault-name-caret` in the loaded plugin, while the source had already moved on.

Do not send him through a restart for a change that exists only in the TypeScript source. When he reports a bug, fix it. Do not stop after an explanation.
